<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh port shut by dockers' strike.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh port shut by dockers' strike.</headline>
<dateline>KHULNA, Bangladesh 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dockers at Bangladesh's Mongla port stopped work on Wednesday and walked out over a wage dispute, port officials said.</p>
<p>They said 6,500 workers began their indefinite strike after talks on 11 demands, including higher wages and benefits and employment for more dock labourers, failed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>At least 12 ships carrying fertiliser, cement and general cargo were at the port awaiting loading and unloading on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Negotiations are still going on to persuade the workers to return to their jobs,&quot; one official said.</p>
</text>
